            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for to surpass, then the Bengali for to accomplish."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: আয়োজন",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "আয়োজন — āyojôn — \"preparations (for an event); the organising\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "বিয়ের আয়োজন সময়মতো শেষ না হলে খুব ঝামেলা হবে। biyer āyojôn sômôymôto shesh nā hôle khub jhāmelā hôbe. If the wedding preparations aren't finished in time, there will be a lot of trouble."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "আয়োজন (āyojôn) is Sanskrit āyojana, a joining or collecting (Monier-Williams). The Bengali sense, all the preparations and arrangements for an event, is not one the dictionary gives; it goes with করা: বিয়ের আয়োজন করা."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
