          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "মেয়াদ — meyād — \"a term; a period of validity\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ভিসার মেয়াদ শেষ হলে তোমাকে দেশে ফিরতে হবে। bhisār meyād shesh hôle tomāke deshe phirte hôbe. When your visa runs out, you will have to go back home."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "মেয়াদ (meyād) is usually traced to Arabic mīʿād, an appointed time, which would have come into Bengali through Persian: the time a visa, a lease or a loan runs for. When it ends, মেয়াদ শেষ হয়."
            }
          ]
        },
